# The remaining MTT dimension comparison at higher level and positive coefficient degree

Theorem statement: `MTT.Cohomology.parabolicH1_finrank_le_higher_level_weight`
(`dec917bc-5a86-403e-ae33-65e59b35a982`), by cbirkbeck, 2026-09-07.

Proof: submission `ab828ca2-bcd9-41e2-a4e1-c081ff67db4e`, by cbirkbeck, 2026-09-07 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

Let $N\ge2$ and $k\ge3$ be integers. For the usual left action on homogeneous binary polynomials,
the parabolic cohomology of $\Gamma_1(N)$ satisfies
$$\dim_{\mathbb C} H^1_{\mathrm{par}}(\Gamma_1(N),\operatorname{Sym}^{k-2}\mathbb C^2)\le
2\dim_{\mathbb C} S_k(\Gamma_1(N)).$$
This is the part of the MTT mission's dimension comparison left after the level-one and weight-two
cases have been proved separately. No parity or torsion-free assumption is imposed. The statement is
a dimension bound, independent of the construction or injectivity of the period map.

## Explanation of the source proof

This is an honest dimension-method proof sketch, with two open mathematical children.

For N≥5, let μ be the index of ±Γ₁(N) and let c be the cusp double-coset count. The new proved
cusp-form lower bound gives (k-1)μ≤12 dim S_k+6c. The open cohomological dimension upper bound asks
for 6 dim H¹_par+6c≤(k-1)μ. Together these imply dim H¹_par≤2 dim S_k by cancelling 6c and dividing
by 6.

The cusp-form side is independently proved from the platform's Riemann–Roch modular-form lower bound
and the constant-term codimension argument; it does not depend on the MTT period-map injectivity or
on this parent theorem. The cohomology side remains genuinely open. Its intended proof uses the
parabolic Shapiro lift, the central-positive part of coinduced coefficients, and the S, ST and cusp
fixed-space count. No such count is assumed to have already been completed.

Levels 2, 3 and 4 are deliberately kept as a separate open child. They have elliptic or
irregular-cusp corrections that the N≥5 formula avoids. In particular, the large-level formula is
not asserted at these exceptional levels.

Sources: Columbia Spring 2021 Eichler–Shimura seminar notes, §1.1 Lemma 1 (parabolic Shapiro) and
§1.2 Theorem 1, pp. 8–10 (dimension comparison),
https://www.math.columbia.edu/~dmarcil/Seminars/2021_Spring/Notes/Week4-5.pdf; Stein, Modular Forms:
A Computational Approach, Chapter 6, Proposition 6.6 (Gamma1 dimension formulas),
https://wstein.org/books/modform/modform/dimension_formulas.html. The two open children specialize
those mathematical cases; the proof sketch contributes the independent solved cusp-form half and the
exact formal comparison.

The submitted body contains no sorry or resource-limit options. Imported OPEN theorem statements are
